  ('mt-bachelor-oregon', '12A', 'Mt. Bachelor', 'United States', 'Oregon''s volcano mountain', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'The Pacific Northwest', '{"ski","culinary","family","ultra","romance","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'anchor', '{"key_facts":["Largest ski resort in the Pacific Northwest (~4,323 acres per resort claim; ''true skiable'' cited ~3,683 elsewhere) — bills itself 2nd-largest single-mountain resort in the US behind Vail","A stratovolcano (cinder cone) with a summit lift opening 360 degrees of terrain; summit 9,065 ft, base ~5,700 ft, vertical ~3,365 ft","One of the longest seasons in North America (late Nov-late May; 2025/26 opened 28 Nov 2025); on the Ikon Pass (7 days Ikon / 5 days Ikon Base); owned by POWDR Corp","POWDR announced 4 Apr 2025 it will retain Mt. Bachelor indefinitely (earlier possible-sale process ended)","Minimal on-mountain lodging; Bend (~22 mi/~30 min via Cascade Lakes Hwy) is the basecamp — Bend Ale Trail, Deschutes River, Tetherow + Sunriver Resort","COAC covers the backcountry zone; RDM (Redmond) ~30 mi; St. Charles Bend nearest ER (Level II trauma)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/ambulance/rescue dispatch, nationwide)","hospital":"St. Charles Bend (Bend, 24/7 ER + Level II trauma, ~30 min); ski-injury clinic at mountain base in season; backcountry via Deschutes County Sheriff SAR / 911","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"ALTITUDE (base ~5,700 ft, summit 9,065 ft — highest in cluster; real but moderate AMS risk) acclimatize/hydrate; AVALANCHE beyond ropes (heavy maritime snowpack; check COAC, guide + beacon/probe/shovel); exposed VOLCANIC SUMMIT holds on wind + fast whiteouts; Cascade winter driving + ODOT chain control (Cascade Lakes Hwy/TripCheck); tree wells + deep snow; cold + fast Pacific storms","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","read":"2026-09-01T16:18:24Z","page_updated"