  ('snowbird-utah', '12A', 'Snowbird', 'United States', 'Ride the tram to Hidden Peak', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Utah Canyon Country', '{"adventure","culinary","entertainment","expedition","family","romance","ski","wellness"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Snowbird = Little Cottonwood Canyon, Ikon Pass PARTNER (note: partner, NOT Alterra-owned; a POWDR ''Adventure Lifestyle Brands'' association surfaced via Powderbird - verify owner); opened Dec 1971 (Ted Johnson + Dick Bass)","The Aerial Tram to Hidden Peak (~11,000 ft, ~2,900 ft rise) is the signature lift; ~2,500 acres, ~3,240 ft vertical, ~149-169 trails; ~35% expert (steep, advanced-leaning); no night skiing","~500 in snow (''Greatest Snow on Earth'', record 776 in May 2011); one of the LONGEST seasons in NA (past Memorial Day, occasionally into July on upper terrain)","SNOWBOARDING ALLOWED (unlike ski-only Alta up-canyon); Peruvian Tunnel -> Mineral Basin links toward Alta; joint Alta-Snowbird ticket since 2002","Wasatch Powderbird Guides (''Powderbird'') heli-skiing operates in ASSOCIATION with Snowbird (powderbird.com -> snowbird.com); NO dedicated on-site snowcat","A purpose-built RESORT base (not a town) at ~7,760 ft; landmark concrete Cliff Lodge (+ Cliff Spa), The Lodge at Snowbird, Iron Blosam Lodge, The Inn; SLC ~29 mi / ~45 min via SR-210 (canyon permitting)","US-TRAFFIC CANDOR: high-volume powder-driven; canyon congestion on storm mornings; no per-resort count published - consensus only","NO natural hot springs (Little Cottonwood is a protected drinking-water watershed - dogs banned); Ikon/lift/Alta-Bird prices dynamic; CANYON SAFETY SPINE: SR-210 traction law (>=5/32 in tread, Class Three), UDOT avalanche closures, INTERLODGE (legal indoor confinement during avalanche control)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/medical/rescue dispatch); alert ski patrol on-mountain","hospital":"No in-canyon hospital - full-service ERs down-canyon in Salt Lake valley (~45 min via SR-210, canyon-access permitting); verify nearest facility","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"ALTITUDE (base ~7,760 ft, Hidden Peak ~11,000 ft - tram takes you high fast; hydrate, ease alcohol, descend if AMS worsens); AVALANCHE life-safety spine (in-bounds patrolled/controlled; beyond ropes severe) - Utah Avalanche Center (UAC) ''Salt Lake'' region - VERIFY exact zone (UAC page 403); beacon/probe/shovel + guide, never duck ropes; SR-210 TRACTION LAW (>=5/32 in tread, enforceable up to 24h pre-storm, Class Three in major storms) + UDOT avalanche closures + INTERLODGE (legal indoor confinement during control - follow lodge/UDOT instructions; exact legal mechanism verify); tree-wells; cold + intense UV","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/usa","read":"2026-09-01T16:18:24Z","page_updated":"2026-08-18T10:29:04+01:00","source_country":"usa","quotes_note":"not extracted by the join — a restricted-area clause is quoted by a human, never composed"},"posture":"book-freely"},"timing":{"peak":"Deep winter + storm/powder days (Christmas/NY, Presidents'' Week, any big storm cycle); long spring (Memorial Day+) a distinctive secondary peak","shoulder":"early season (Dec), Jan midweek, late spring after holidays","green":"summer + fall (scenic tram, hiking, Oktoberfest) + Oct-Nov lull","booking_lead":"Christmas/NY + Presidents'' + Cliff Lodge peak 3-6 mo; storm-chasing powder trips opportunistic (short lead); Ikon by early fall","off_season_specials":"long spring skiing; summer tram + hiking; autumn Oktoberfest; midweek value","event_peaks":"Christmas/NY, MLK + Presidents'', spring-skiing events, autumn Oktoberfest (verify dates)","fire_date":"FIRE spring early-bird (Apr-Jun) Ikon renewals + long-spring push; fire again Sep-Nov + storm-triggered powder alerts"},"jewels":[{"name":"Ride the Aerial Tram to Hidden Peak","status":"live","tier":"comfort","price_ban