  ('stevens-pass-washington', '12A', 'Stevens Pass', 'United States', 'Deep Cascade powder two hours from Seattle', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'The Pacific Northwest', '{"ski","family","culinary","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'core', '{"key_facts":["Cascade-crest day-use mountain on US-2, ~65 mi/~2 hr NE of Seattle; Vail Resorts-operated (acquired 2018), on the Epic Pass (unlimited)","~1,125 skiable acres, 52 trails, 13 lifts, base 4,061 ft / summit 5,845 ft / ~1,784 ft vertical, ~460 in avg snowfall; ~11% beginner / 54% intermediate / 35% advanced","7th Heaven Chair (two-seat Riblet) billed as America''s steepest lift; Mill Valley ''backside'' (min elev ~3,821 ft)","Night skiing Wed-Sun to 10 p.m.; no slopeside village (day lodges: Granite Peaks Lodge + Creek Lodge)","Stevens Pass Nordic Center: ~30 km groomed classic/skate + ~10 km snowshoe, Lower Mill Valley ~5 mi east (Cascade Depot, Thu-Sun)","Leavenworth (Bavarian village ~35 mi east on US-2) = lodging/culinary/romance base; Christmas Lighting + Oktoberfest town-scale peaks","2025/26 opened Dec 5, 2025; Tunnel Creek backcountry (off-boundary) is serious avalanche terrain (2012 fatal slide)"],"safety":{"emergency":"911 (police/fire/ambulance/rescue dispatch, nationwide)","hospital":"Nearest ERs: Cascade Medical (Leavenworth, critical-access, ~35 mi E); EvergreenHealth Monroe (~40 mi W); Confluence Health/Central Washington Hospital (Wenatchee, larger trauma, ~35 mi SE); serious cases transfer to Wenatchee/Seattle; backcountry via county SAR / 911","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"WSDOT US-2 pass driving + Caltrans-style chain control + winter-long avalanche control (''Old Faithful'' zone, closures held at summit MP64/Scenic MP56); AVALANCHE beyond ropes incl. Tunnel Creek zone (NWAC bulletin, guide + beacon/probe/shovel); heavy maritime ''Cascade Concrete'' + tree-well/snow-immersion risk; fast Pacific storms/whiteout + wind-hold (